# google-finance-scraper — copy to .env and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED to scrape this site, and on this one that is
# unusually strong. Measured 2026-09-22 from a datacentre address in Helsinki
# with no key, no proxy and no account:
#
#   --mode markets --market US    46 rows, every one priced
#   --mode movers  --market US    11 rows
#   --mode quote   x 4 symbols     4 rows, 8.3 seconds
#
# The market is a QUERY PARAMETER on this site, not a property of your exit
# address — `--market US` from a Finnish address returns NASDAQ movers and
# CBOE sector indices — so the usual reason to buy an exit does not apply
# here. Everything below buys volume or resilience, not access.
#
# A credential belongs in this file and NEVER on a command line: anything
# that can run `ps` can read an argv, and shell history keeps it.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any of it:
#
#   python3 env_config.py
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#   an explicit flag  ->  an exported environment variable  ->  .env  ->  the
#   default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file someone forgot to delete.

# --- 2Captcha, one key for four separately-billed products ---------------
# Solving, the Scraping Browser API, proxies and fingerprints all sit behind
# this one key. https://2captcha.com/enterpage
#
# No captcha was met on this site in testing: every candidate marker scored
# ZERO across 11 captures, served and refused alike. That is a measurement
# from one address on one day and NOT a claim that Google does not challenge
# scrapers — it serves /sorry/index with a reCAPTCHA to addresses it scores
# badly, this repo recognises that page, and 2Captcha solves that task type.
# Detection stays wired for the day it fires.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- The Scraping Browser API (a managed browser over CDP) ---------------
# The endpoint SHAPE, not a working endpoint: a profile's credentials live
# about a day, so anything pasted here is stale by tomorrow and produces an
# auth error a long way from its cause. Get fresh ones from the dashboard.
#
#   country-xx  picks the exit country.
#   pid-...     is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection
#               each, so reuse pids rather than minting one per run, and do
#               not raise --concurrency above 1 with this set.
#
# Do NOT add --fingerprint or a custom user agent on top of this: the remote
# browser already has an identity, and stacking a second one creates a
# contradiction rather than better cover. The engines ignore the flag with
# --cdp-endpoint and say so.
GOOGLE_FINANCE_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-us-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- A proxy exit --------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to reach a named market — use --market for that. Worth having
# for VOLUME, where spreading a run across exits is what keeps any one
# address from being scored.
#
# The host below is the documented SHAPE. Take the real one from the
# dashboard — the `{...}` parts are what you fill in, and env_config treats
# any value still containing braces as unset, so a copied example is never
# sent to the API as if it were a credential.
GOOGLE_FINANCE_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@us.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- A default URL ------------------------------------------------------
# Saves typing `--url` on every run. An explicit --url always wins, and
# --symbols wins over both in --mode quote.
GOOGLE_FINANCE_URL=https://www.google.com/finance/quote/GOOGL:NASDAQ

# --- A default market ---------------------------------------------------
# Two letters, sent as Google's own `gl`. Load-bearing for --mode markets and
# --mode movers, whose lists are geo-selected.
GOOGLE_FINANCE_MARKET=US
